{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Carve for yourself.</b> He showed him a quarry of sapphire from inside his tent and said to him: the chips shall be yours; from there Moses became very wealthy (Tanchuma)." "<b>Carve for yourself.</b> You shattered the first ones — you carve others for yourself. A parable: a king who went to a maritime province and left his bride among the maidservants; through the corruption of the maidservants a bad name went out about her. The matchmaker arose and tore up her marriage contract. He said: if the king says to put her to death, I will say to him: she is not yet your wife. The king investigated and found that the corruption was only on account of the maidservants, and was reconciled to her. The matchmaker said to him: write her another marriage contract, for the first was torn. The king said to him: you tore it — you acquire paper for her yourself and I shall write for her in my own hand. So too — the king, this is the Holy One, blessed be He; the maidservants, these are the mixed multitude; the matchmaker, this is Moses; the bride of the Holy One, blessed be He, is Israel. Therefore it says: ״פְּסָל לְךָ״ (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:29.257908467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}